Their response consisted only of a billing invoice and transaction history, which failed to include a signed contract, proof of debt ownership, accurate itemization, or any verifiable evidence that the alleged balance is correct and collectible. Moreover, the billing history clearly shows that the account was charged off and reduced to a {$0.00} balance as of XX/XX/XXXX. Their attempt to re-age and inflate the debt to over {$1100.00} in XXXX constitutes an illegal attempt to collect on a time-barred and previously settled or charged-off account.

