14513608,2025-07-08,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"I am filing this complaint in response to three charge-off accounts that are currently being reported on my XXXX, Equifax, and XXXX  credit reports : XXXX XXXX ( Account # : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX  ), XXXX XXXX  XXXX XXXX Account # : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ), and XXXX  ( Account # : XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX ). These accounts are being reported with derogatory charge-off statuses {$2300.00}, {$4900.00}, and {$15000.00} XXXX XXXX respectivelybut none of them should remain on my credit reports at this point, nor should they carry such damaging and outdated notations. 

These accounts are not only over a decade old in some cases, but theyve been settled, paid, or resolved through previous disputes. I have made every effort to clean up and maintain an accurate credit profile, not just for my financial health, but also for the stability of my family and long-term goals. Seeing these outdated charge-offs still appearingafter so many years and after taking the proper stepsfeels like a slap in the face. Its as if no matter how much work I put into building my credit back up, Im still being dragged down by errors or negligence from the very systems that are supposed to protect consumers. 

