The Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), under 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ), requires credit bureaus to maintain maximum possible accuracy in all consumer reporting. Once a dispute has been submitted, they are also bound under 15 U.S.C. 1681i to reinvestigate the item thoroughly. If the account can not be verified with current, accurate documentation, then it must be removed or corrected. Simply leaving the burden on the consumer indefinitely is not just unfairits unlawful.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",IA,50320,,Web,2025-07-08,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
