14624398,2025-07-13,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Overcharged for something you did purchase with the card,"XX/XX/XXXX Consumer Financial Protection Bureau XXXX. XXXX XXXX XXXX, IA XXXX Subject : Complaint Against Capital One for Unfair Denial of Dispute Case Number : * * * Dear CFPB, I am filing a complaint against Capital One Financial Corp for the wrongful denial of my dispute for a {$240.00} charge on my account ( ending XXXX ) by XXXX XXXX on XX/XX/XXXX, posted XX/XX/XXXX, for an expedited e-visa to XXXX required by XXXX Airlines ( PAL ). Capital Ones denial, dated XX/XX/XXXX, cites the dispute exceeding a 45-day Mastercard processing limit and my alleged failure to provide a transaction receipt or evidence of attempting to resolve the issue with the merchant. This denial misapplies Mastercard rules, ignores my diligent pursuit, and fails to address coercion and misrepresentation by PAL and WORLD TRAVEL, violating fair lending practices under the Dodd-Frank Act. I seek full restitution of the {$240.00} charge. 
Background of the Dispute : On XX/XX/XXXX, PAL denied me boarding as a XXXX citizen unless I paid {$240.00} to XXXX XXXX XXXXor an expedited e-visa, under extreme time pressure ( 30 minutes before my flight ). PAL failed to inform me during booking or thereafter of XXXX XXXX requirement, which I could have obtained for {$25.00} {$28.00} via the official portal ( evisa.xuatnhapcanh.gov.vn ). The {$240.00} charge, a 980 % markup, constitutes predatory pricing. PAL directed me to a XXXX XXXX representative via phone, offering no alternative, suggesting coercion and possible collusion, as XXXX XXXX may be a PAL affiliate or subsidiary. 

