2. No Separate Receipt : Capital One claims I failed to provide a receipt. XXXX XXXX provided no separate receipt, typical for airport-based electronic services. My credit card statement, showing the {$240.00} charge to XXXX XXXX  was submitted and suffices as transaction evidence under Mastercard rules ( XXXX, XXXX ). Capital Ones demand for a separate receipt is unreasonable. 

3. Merchant Resolution Attempts : I informed Capital One during the initial dispute ( XX/XX/XXXX ) and in my appeal letter that I called XXXX XXXX three times ( using a number provided by PAL at check-in, approximately late XX/XX/XXXX ) with no response. This demonstrates a good-faith attempt, as required by Mastercard ( XXXX, XXXX ). Capital One dismissed this without requesting further details ( e.g., call logs, available if needed ). 

