14870268,2025-07-24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"b""To Whom It May Concern,\n\nI am filing this complaint to report a serious and harmful inaccuracy related to a XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  credit card account that is currently damaging my credit profile due to unlawful reporting practices.\n\nThis account was charged off, yet it is being reported in violation of the following:\n\n1.  Violation of the CARES Act (Public Law 116-136)\nThe CARES Act, effective XXXX XXXX XXXX through XXXX XXXX XXXX, amended the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA) under Section 4021, requiring furnishers to pause negative credit reporting for accounts under accommodation due to COVID-19 hardship.\n\nDuring this time, I experienced financial hardship due to the pandemic and was entitled to protection from adverse credit reporting. Despite this, XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX reported my account as delinquent and ultimately charged off the account in XXXX XXXX, which violated the law during an active CARES protection window.\n\n2.  Illegal Re-Aging of Charge-Off (FCRA  605(c)  15 U.S.C.  1681c)\nEven more concerning, XXXX XXXX  re-aged the charge-off by continuing to report the account as newly delinquent from XXXX XXXX through XXXX XXXX, falsely making the account appear more recent and more damaging than it actually is.\n\nUnder the FCRA:\n\nThe Date of First Delinquency (DOFD) governs the reporting period for derogatory items. Re-aging the delinquency date or updating the account in a way that misrepresents the original default is strictly prohibited under 15 U.S.C.  1681c(a)(4).\n\XXXX XXXX monthly updates to this charge-off are misleading and suggest ongoing activity where none exists, which illegally extends the damage to my credit score and falsely resets the accounts reporting life cycle.\n\n Requested Resolution:\nI am requesting the following corrective action:\n\nThe negative XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX charge account be deleted because of its' illegal reporting;\n\nIf the account was reported during CARES Act protection due to hardship, then the entire charge-off entry must be removed as a violation of federal law;\n\nProvide written confirmation and a corrected credit report upon completion of the investigation.\n\nThis inaccurate and unlawful reporting has directly harmed my ability to access credit, housing, and fair financial opportunities.\n\nPlease escalate this complaint and provide a resolution in accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act and the CARES Act.\n\nSincerely,\nXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",SC,29607,,Web,2025-07-24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
