14870556,2025-07-26,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I sent two dispute letters to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX IL XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX CA XXXX ), and Equifax ( XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX, GA XXXX ) on or around XX/XX/XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXX, respectively, pursuant to my rights under the FCRA ( 15 USC 1681i ) and the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA, 15 USC 1692g ). These letters detailed multiple inaccuracies, incomplete information, and unverifiable items related to the XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX account, as outlined below : Inaccurate Account Status and Payment Status ( Violation of 15 USC 1681e ( b ) and 15 USC 1681i ) XXXX reports the account as "" Closed '' with a payment status of "" Charged off as bad debt, '' a balance and past due amount of {$17000.00}, a "" Date of Last Payment '' of XX/XX/XXXX, and a "" Date Last Active '' of XX/XX/XXXX. 
