14986603,2025-07-30,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Old information reappears or never goes away,"Im filing this complaint because TransUnion has once again violated my rights under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), specifically 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) and 1681i ( 5 ) ( B ) ( ii )- ( iii ), by reinserting this account that was already deleted from my credit report earlier this year. 

XXXX Card XXXX I disputed this account way back on XX/XX/year>, and they confirmed the deletion, and in fact, they sent me a letter. Experian sent me a letter dated XX/XX/year>, stating that this account was DELETED from my file. I have that letter and will include it as an attachment. So what was that? A mistake? A joke? Or just a display to shut me up? Because now, months later, that same account is back on my credit report, with no explanation, no documentation, and definitely no notice within the XXXX requirement outlined under 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( 5 ) ( B ).

The FCRA requires two things before reinserting any deleted information : A certification from the furnisher that the info is accurate and complete. 

A written notice to me within XXXX business days of the reinsertion, explaining what was reinserted, who reported it, and that I have the right to dispute it again. 

TransUnion did neither. I didnt get a notice. I didnt get the name, address, or phone number of the furnisher. I didnt even get told that it was being reinserted at all. So what kind of reinvestigation did they do? Because it looks like they just copy or rubber-stamped this through XXXX like always, marked it verified, and hoped I wouldnt notice. 

Thats NOT how this is supposed to work. This kind of sloppy and lazy reinsertion violates the FCRAs requirement for maximum possible accuracy under 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ). If TransUnion cant even follow the basic legal steps to reinvestigate or explain why this account is back on my report, how am I supposed to trust anything they report? Theres no transparency. No accountability. Just silence and unverified data. 

I want this account PERMANENTLY DELETED AND NEVER ADDED AGAIN. Not just temporarily removed. I also want TransUnion to provide the full reinvestigation record, including who verified this account, what documents were used, and how they determined this account was legitimate. If they cant give me that, then they have no business reporting it in the first place.

Lastly, Im demanding that TransUnion be held accountable for this. Reinserting an account without notice is a direct FCRA violation, and under 15 U.S.C. 1681n and 1681o, they can be held liable for at least {$1000.00} per violation if done willfully. At this point, it sure feels willful.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",NJ,07032,,Web,2025-07-30,Closed with explanation,Yes
